#!ipxe
#
# Embedded into our own custom iPXE build (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and
# scripts/build-ipxe.sh) -- replaces netboot.xyz entirely. netboot.xyz was
# only ever providing one thing in this project: a way to reach an iPXE
# prompt. Everything past that point (the boot script, hook, bridge,
# kernel/initrd, the ISO itself) has been on our own static hosting for a
# while now, so there's no reason left to depend on netboot.xyz's binary,
# menu, or asset mirror at all -- this IS our own iPXE, built from the
# same open-source project netboot.xyz builds on top of, boots straight
# here with zero menu, zero manual keypresses.

echo Booting Omarchy netboot (no netboot.xyz)...
dhcp || goto shell
chain https://lagsoftware.com/files/omarchy-nbd.ipxe || goto shell
goto shell

:shell
echo Chain failed, or you asked for the shell -- dropping to iPXE shell.
shell
